  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 136 PM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nShortwave ridging reaches TX to make for a fine day of fair\nweather skies developing by Wednesday afternoon. The warmest day\nof the week will be a short warm pattern, because by Wednesday\nevening, another cold front arrives after polar troughing \nsharpens up over the eastern CONUS. Cool and generally dry\nconditions will follow the front through Friday night. Then for\ndaytime Saturday, a zonal pattern overhead brings the next\nshortwave trough and enough Pacific moisture to bring more good\nrain chances to South TX.",
